          {
           "type": "heading",
           "level": 2,
           "html": "Ada",
           "align": "center",
           "size": null
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "html": "<strong>Ada</strong>’s world within the Imaginarium is a meticulous mesh of linear perspective, inspired by masters like Sebastiano Serlio and Vredeman de Vries, reflecting their systematic and precise approach to creating life on Venus. This love for architectural and perspective drawings underscores Ada’s methodical nature and their fascination with constructing environments where organic and mechanical elements intertwine seamlessly. Through these influences, Ada envisions and engineers complex terraforming projects on Venus, each a testament to the potential of combining art, science, and imagination.",
           "align": null,
           "size": null
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
